// 💡 BEST FLOW (REAL WORLD)
// On login:
// Get all user workspaces
// Set one as active
// Store it (cookie/session)
// On route access:
// Get workspace from URL
// Check DB → does user belong?
// If NO → block
// If YES → allow
// ❌ WHAT NOT TO DO

// ❌ Trust URL blindly
// ❌ Only use localStorage
// ❌ Skip backend validation

// 👉 That leads to security issues

// 💯 FINAL ARCHITECTURE
// Route → Extract workspace slug
//       → Validate in DB (workspaceMembers)
//       → Allow or block
// 🔥 DEFENSE ANSWER

// If asked:

// “How do you prevent unauthorized workspace access?”

// Say:

// “The system validates workspace access by checking user membership against the database. Even if a user manipulates the URL, access is restricted unless they belong to that workspace.”

// 💥 That’s a top-tier answer

